---
import "../styles/app.css";
import Head from "../components/Head.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import data from "../data/registry.json";

// The home page: what this is in the middle, the ways in on the left, what
// arrived recently on the right.
//
// PROSE IS PLACEHOLDER. The sentences in the middle column are lifted from
// BRIEF.md so the page says something true in the author's own words rather than
// in mine. Replace them before anyone outside sees this.

// Named from the data, so the exception in the banner cannot outlive the rows
// that make it true. Same construction as layouts/Base.astro.
const owned = (data.real_authors ?? []).map((n) => n + "'s");
const exception =
  owned.length === 0
    ? ""
    : owned.length === 1
      ? owned[0]
      : owned.slice(0, -1).join(", ") + " and " + owned[owned.length - 1];

const recent = data.model_index
  .flatMap((m) => m.submissions)
  .slice()
  .sort((a, b) => b.created_at.localeCompare(a.created_at))
  .slice(0, 8);

const released = (iso) =>
  new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" });

const belowThreshold = data.corpus.size < data.corpus.threshold;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head title="controlbun" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteNav />

    <div class="home">
      <nav class="sidenav">
        <h3>Browse</h3>
        <a href="/models/">Models</a>
        <a href="/owners/">Owners</a>

        <h3>Account</h3>
        <span class="soon">Profile</span>
        <span class="soon">Submissions</span>
        <span class="soon">Settings</span>

        <h3>Resources</h3>
        <span class="soon">Getting started</span>
        <span class="soon">Documentation</span>
        <span class="soon">Publishing a submission</span>

      </nav>

      <main class="intro">
        {data.any_synthetic && (
          <div class="banner">
            <strong>Synthetic corpus{exception ? `, except ${exception}` : ""}.</strong>{" "}
            {exception
              ? `Every submission listed here is fabricated to exercise the interface apart from ${exception}, which is a real direction with real measurements. Fabricated scores are repeated-digit decimals, fabricated vectors are integer ramps, and the models those name do not resolve.`
              : "Every submission listed here is fabricated to exercise the interface. Scores are repeated-digit decimals, vectors are integer ramps, and the models named do not resolve. Nothing on this site is a measurement."}
          </div>
        )}

        <h1>controlbun</h1>

        <p class="lede">
          A registry for activation-steering artifacts, in the spirit of GitHub or
          Hugging Face rather than a curated database.
        </p>

        {/* Short on purpose. The long argument moved to /about/ on 2026-09-13,
            split by first visit rather than by topic: someone arriving cold needs
            the next paragraph or they read every page after it as a leaderboard,
            and by the fifth visit an essay on the home page is furniture.

            The plurality claim stays here because misreading it is the one failure
            that makes the rest of the site unreadable. Everything else is a
            deliberate read, once, and lives on /about/.

            PROSE STILL PLACEHOLDER, lifted from BRIEF.md. It is true and it is in
            the author's words, but it was written for a design brief and not for
            someone landing here cold. */}
        <p>
          Ten people will extract <span class="mono">kindness</span> with different
          contrast data, different theories of what kindness is, and different ideas
          about what could be confounding it. This holds all ten side by side and
          makes the disagreement legible. It does not pick a winner, mandate a
          definition, or impose a single evaluation.
        </p>

        <p>
          The primary object is a submission: one author's complete take,
          self-contained, comparable to others after the fact rather than conformant
          to them in advance. <a href="/about/">What this is and where it came
          from</a>.
        </p>

      </main>

      <aside class="rail">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>{belowThreshold ? "Recently added" : "Trending"}</h3>
          <ol>
            {recent.map((s) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`/${s.author}/${s.model_id}/${s.label}/${s.version}/`}>
                  {s.author}/{s.label}
                </a>
                <span class="meta mono">{s.kind} · {s.model_id}</span>
                <span class="meta">{released(s.created_at)}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="why">
            {belowThreshold
              ? `${data.corpus.size} submissions, under the ${data.corpus.threshold} needed before engagement means anything. Newest first until then: there is nothing to trend on yet, and an invented ranking would be worse than none.`
              : "Evaluations and attacks by people other than the author, decayed by age. Never a measured score, and not downloads."}
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

  </body>
</html>
